                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is kind of okay...at best.\n\nThe colored pencil artwork in phenomenal and I wish they did that in like a Yoshi game or something where the devs would be more competent. While it looks nice, it makes it very hard to tell what you can stand on or not.\n\nThere's random people scattered throughout the levels so I never knew if someone was an enemy or just a pointless piece of scenery when first seeing that particular design.\n\nThe gameplay itself is okay, but has a lot of issues that would take too long to explain, so I'll just point at the most frustrating--you can't attack in midair. So many enemies are positioned in places that you can really only hit them after jumping. So instead you're forced to jump into them first to get on even ground. Simply put, air attacks would have made this so much better.\n\nThe game is pretty easy. The bosses are kinda crap and really annoying until you figure out how to beat them.\nBut then you get to the last boss and he's impossible unless you grind cold coins to upgrade your stats to max and also find a bunch of objects hidden throughout the levels.\nBut the game isn't fun enough to want to explore the mostly crappy level design that isn't at all straightforward a lot of the time. I'm sure you can get away with beating the game easily enough without finding all this stuff, and the second to last level makes grinding tolerable, but again, the game's not fun enough to want to do that. If the whole game is so easy, why toss in this huge hurdle?\n\nI'd pass on this.\n",
